  "note": "Extracted by hand from the ordering schematic, the 95 head with the gauge port left blank when not needed. The body Cv rows carry printed size brackets, all 1/2 inch on the B row, and the o-ring and diaphragm tables split at 1.2 Cv by their own brackets, all enforced. The 3-8 range's footnote says it must use the EPDM/Nylon diaphragm; no diaphragm row of that name is printed on this sheet, so the plain Jorlon rows are refused and the naming is held for John. The trims with no body Cv row of their own, the 0.3 and 1.2 Cv seats, are matched to the all-half-inch B body as an inferred coupling. The sheet's deadhead warning against metal seats rides the hard seat rows as a caution.",
